    "notes": "Reviewed 2026-10-07. Fidelity Digital Assets, National Association is the sole FIDD issuer and USD redemption obligor. OCC active-trust-bank list as of August 31, 2026 names charter 25398; NYDFS confirms conversion effective December 12, 2025. Existing federal-qualified-nonbank pathway records the statutory route for an uninsured national bank, not an attained PPSI authorization. OCC December 12 decision conditions 3 and 5 distinguish future GENIUS compliance and separate written nonobjection for a bank-issued stablecoin from ordinary charter approval. No public section 5 GENIUS approval or official GENIUS application was located. February 4 issuer launch commentary describes GENIUS regulatory clarity but does not announce a formal PPSI application. Latest opened PwC examination dated September 25, 2026 addresses August 7 and 31 reserves and explicitly does not examine legal/regulatory compliance. Removed stale categorical assertions that no approval framework or PPSI approvals exist anywhere.",
